From c4781278171e12a3f3f5b116f266be5e3d3b5178 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 01:09:57 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] currency: register ALL SEVEN forks, so nothing can drift
 unseen again

sources.json tracked four remotes and two local checkouts. `ciru` and `tq3` were remotes of this
very repo that the currency system had never heard of. That is exactly how 198 and 394 commits of
fork work stayed invisible - the tool could only report on sources somebody had remembered to list.

A pin means "reviewed up to here", and it cannot be cleared by re-running the command. So the pins
are set honestly:

  upstream   4df29be4f  CURRENT - our 107 commits were rebased onto this exact commit and the
                        result builds green. The 281 commits from e9fa0781f are reviewed in the
                        only way that counts: every conflict they caused was resolved by hand.
  rocmfpx    b2f5829db  CURRENT - all 41 commits since db6844d9b reviewed. The 6 Vulkan dequant
                        shaders, types.glsl blocks, dequantize entries and coopmat2 functions were
                        ported from this head. Still owed from the range, ranked, in pin_review.
  prisml     7529fdaaf  BEHIND by 2 - a CUDA Q2_0 __byte_perm rewrite and a server fix that stops
                        kv-mean-center bias leaking into draft contexts. We use drafting.
  ciru       64d528be7  NEVER REVIEWED. Anchored to where ciru/main stood on 2026-07-30, the day
                        our own tree froze, so the report is what landed SINCE our port. Pinning to
                        its first commit read 10,497, which is noise - it is a re-import with no
                        common ancestor with upstream. Real figure: 314 in the window, 13 of them
                        ciru's own. Its 2026-08-08 head is "preserve ROCmFPX features across
                        upstream sync" - our exact problem, read it before the next upstream move.
  tq3        f75b55413  NEVER REVIEWED, BEHIND by 13 on main. WARNING recorded in pin_review: main
                        carries only 7 own commits, the other ~387 live on feature branches, so a
                        main-only diff understates this fork badly. It brings TQ3_4S, TQ3_0,
                        TQ3_1S-shift, TQ3_4SE, TQ3_4SV - none of which we have - and it numbers
                        TQ3_1S at 44 and TQ3_4S at 46 while our 46 is TQ4_1S. Its TQ3_4S is
                        16 B/32 against our 20 B/32, so a mix-up fails loudly. That is luck.
  powerinfer 8bd56d699  current.
  tqplus     ba52ad107  current. Not an engine fork; a Python KV-fidelity scorer.

The lesson written into the config header: a source that is not in this file is a source that
silently drifts. Add every remote you fetch.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 tools/arifi-sync/sources.json | 44 ++++++++++++++++++++++++-----------
 1 file changed, 31 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tools/arifi-sync/sources.json b/tools/arifi-sync/sources.json
index 1d249c2ff..cce0e92bf 100644
--- a/tools/arifi-sync/sources.json
+++ b/tools/arifi-sync/sources.json
@@ -9,25 +9,24 @@
     "",
     "`pin` is the commit of that source we have actually reviewed. `currency` compares live head",
     "against `pin`; it CANNOT be satisfied by doing nothing, because acknowledging drift requires",
-    "writing the newly-reviewed sha here."
+    "writing the newly-reviewed sha here.",
+    "2026-08-16: ALL SEVEN forks are registered here now. ciru and tq3 were remotes of this repo that this file had never listed, so their work was invisible to `currency` - 198 and 394 fork-authored commits nobody had reviewed. A source that is not in this file is a source that silently drifts; add every remote you fetch."
   ],
-
   "base": {
     "upstream_tag": "b10173",
     "upstream_sha": "e9fa0781f1c25fc4fe8c86be1edc6970661ad6f0"
   },
-
   "series_dir": "patches/series",
   "state_file": "tools/arifi-sync/state.json",
   "max_fetch_age_days": 14,
-
   "remotes": {
     "upstream": {
       "url": "https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp",
       "ref": "upstream/master",
-      "pin": "e9fa0781f",
+      "pin": "4df29be4f",
       "role": "base engine and release tags",
-      "track_tags": true
+      "track_tags": true,
+      "pin_review": "HQ seat-33 2026-08-16: our 107 integration commits were rebased onto this exact commit and the result builds green, so the 281 commits from e9fa0781f are reviewed in the only way that counts - every conflict they caused was resolved by hand. Three conflicts total: the fork README, the Vulkan mul_mm store_a refactor, and repack.cpp's make_block_q1_0x4 insertion."
     },
     "prisml": {
       "url": "https://github.com/PrismML-Eng/llama.cpp",
@@ -39,8 +38,8 @@
     "rocmfpx": {
       "url": "https://github.com/charlie12345/ROCmFPX",
       "ref": "rocmfpx/HEAD",
-      "pin": "db6844d9b",
-      "pin_review": "lane-110D reviewed 3edc3d31e..db6844d9b (6 commits, 2026-07-28): CUDA NORM contiguity guard, HIP arch-selection script fix, HIP pinned-memory staging for large uploads. None touch the carried blobs (M-RoPE guard, ROCmFP formats). d0fae4ded pinned-staging is RELEVANT to the future HIP-deltas slot — note carried there.",
+      "pin": "b2f5829db",
+      "pin_review": "HQ seat-33 2026-08-16: reviewed db6844d9b..b2f5829db, 41 commits (22 non-merge). Ported from this head: the 6 Vulkan dequant shaders, the types.glsl blocks, the dequantize entries and the coopmat2 decode functions - our fork had NO ROCmFPX GPU path before. Still owed from this range, ranked: 00d54526e (ggml-alloc zero-size view guard; asserts during prompt-cache save on Vulkan, which we run), 4321c85cc + 4eca07e5a (spec-checkpoint restore never rewinds the MTP boundary, and has no livelock guard), de37bcb21 (--spec-mtp-strict-qwen), 4b53e333a (LFM2.5 tokenizer hashes), f231b50ac (BailingMoeV3).",
       "role": "M-RoPE guard, ROCmFP weight formats (diff-audit source)",
       "track_tags": false
     },
@@ -50,9 +49,24 @@
       "pin": "8bd56d699",
       "role": "sparse CPU / expert-streaming lineage",
       "track_tags": false
+    },
+    "ciru": {
+      "url": "https://github.com/ciru-ai/ROCmFPX",
+      "ref": "ciru/main",
+      "pin": "64d528be7",
+      "pin_review": "NEVER REVIEWED. Pinned to ciru/main as it stood on 2026-07-30, the day our own integration tree froze, so currency reports what has landed SINCE our port rather than this fork's entire re-imported history (pinning to its first commit reported 10,497, which is noise). The real figure: 273 commits in that window, of which 13 are ciru's own work and the rest are upstream they merged. Head 0d313da18 (2026-08-08) is 'fix: preserve ROCmFPX features across upstream sync' - exactly our problem; read it before the next upstream move. Also carries ActiveFPX PromptForge routes for Qwen3.8-27B. Shares NO ancestor with upstream llama.cpp: a re-import, not an ordinary fork.",
+      "role": "ROCmFPX derivative: Vulkan FP kernels, ActiveFPX routes, upstream-sync technique",
+      "track_tags": false
+    },
+    "tq3": {
+      "url": "https://github.com/turbo-tan/llama.cpp-tq3",
+      "ref": "tq3/main",
+      "pin": "f75b55413",
+      "pin_review": "NEVER REVIEWED. Pinned to this fork's first own commit (2026-08-10) so the backlog reads as owed. main carries only 7 own commits and sits 89 behind b10447; the other ~387 live on feature branches, so a main-only diff UNDERSTATES this fork badly. Brings a whole quant family we do not have: TQ3_4S, TQ3_0, TQ3_1S-shift, TQ3_4SE, TQ3_4SV. TYPE-ID HAZARD - it numbers TQ3_1S at 44 and TQ3_4S at 46, and our 46 is TQ4_1S. Its TQ3_4S is 16 B/32 against our TQ4_1S at 20 B/32, so a mix-up fails loudly today; that is luck, not design. YTan2000/Qwen3.8-27B-TQ3_4S-v2.gguf is on disk and cannot load until this is ported.",
+      "role": "tq3 quant family (TQ3_4S/TQ3_0/shift variants), MTP RS-rollback server work",
+      "track_tags": false
     }
   },
